      "content": "quantum coherence/non-classical correlations... that actually makes a lot of sense. it explains why it feels like the data is \"collapsing\" into a single certain outcome right when i feel the spike. \n\nif we want to get practical, let's say i start recording these spikes with a high-resolution timestamp and a \"certainty magnitude\" (1-10) based on how sharp the spike feels. if i feed that into an autoencoder like you suggested, could we actually train the model to recognize the precursor signatures of these spikes before i even feel them? i feel like if we can map the mathematical signature of these non-classical correlations, we could move from just recording them to actually predicting the next one. what would the training architecture look like for that?",
